  "caption": "Quinn bought full lycra for a big ride. By kilometre 60, the ring and little fingers had gone to sleep.\n\nNumb hands on the bike are common. Pressure on the heel of the palm plus road buzz can irritate a nerve, especially when too much weight goes through your hands on long or static indoor rides.\n\nWhat often helps: changing hand positions every few minutes with relaxed elbows, a bike fit to balance your weight, padded gloves or bar tape, and building trunk strength so you lean less on the bars.\n\nNumbness lasting more than a day or two, clumsy or weak hands, thinning hand muscles or symptoms off the bike are worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
